[- Tooling: editors + LSP + install scripts. -]
[page id='editors'
  [meta
    title='Editors and LSP'
    layout='reference'
    nav-order='500'
    audience='user'
    summary='Syntax highlighting, completions, diagnostics. One installer script per editor.'
  ]

  [section id='lsp' title='The CX Language Server'
    [prose A single `cx lsp` subcommand speaks LSP over stdio. Any editor that talks LSP can drive completion, hover, go-to-definition, diagnostics, formatting, and rename refactors against CX, CXL, and CXS sources.]
    [code lang='shell' src='cx lsp     # speaks LSP on stdin/stdout']
    [prose The server is built into the cx binary itself — no separate install. Editors point at the cx executable and the server starts on demand.]
  ]

  [section id='install' title='Editor Installers'
    [prose The tooling/install/ directory in the repo ships one shell script per editor. Each script writes the editor config, registers the cx LSP, and drops the syntax-highlighting plugin.]
    [code lang='shell' src='''./tooling/install/install.sh           # interactive — detects editors on PATH
./tooling/install/install-vscode.sh    # VS Code only
./tooling/install/install-nvim.sh      # Neovim only
./tooling/install/install-lsp.sh       # LSP wiring only, no extension
./tooling/install/uninstall.sh         # remove everything''']
  ]

  [section id='vscode' title='VS Code'
    [prose The VS Code extension lives at tooling/vscode. Syntax highlighting is via a tree-sitter grammar (tooling/tree-sitter-cx); LSP integration uses the standard vscode-languageclient harness.]
    [list
      [item path='tooling/editors' label='Syntax highlighting for .cx / .cxl / .cxs files']
      [item path='tooling/editors' label='Diagnostics from cx lint and cx validate']
      [item path='tooling/editors' label='Hover documentation on directives and CXPath functions']
      [item path='tooling/editors' label='Format-on-save via cx fmt']
    ]
  ]

  [section id='neovim' title='Neovim'
    [prose Neovim configuration goes under tooling/neovim. The install script writes the LSP client config into the user runtime path and adds the tree-sitter grammar.]
    [code lang='shell' src='./tooling/install/install-nvim.sh']
  ]

  [section id='other' title='Other Editors'
    [prose Any editor with LSP support can drive cx lsp directly. Point the editor at the cx binary and register .cx, .cxl, and .cxs as the file types. Helix, Emacs (via lsp-mode), Sublime Text (via LSP plugin), and IntelliJ IDEA (via LSP4IJ) all work without further configuration.]
  ]

  [section id='tree-sitter' title='Tree-Sitter Grammar'
    [prose The tooling/tree-sitter-cx grammar is the source of syntax highlighting in every editor. Build with `tree-sitter generate` from the tooling/tree-sitter-cx directory; the prebuilt artifacts ship in the per-editor extensions.]
  ]

  [section id='related' title='Related'
    [list
      [item path='install'            label='Install CX itself']
      [item path='reference/cli'      label='cx lint and cx fmt — the diagnostic backends']
    ]
  ]

  [preserve id='author-notes'
    [- Hand-written notes survive regeneration. Empty by default. -]
  ]
]
